if $f(x,y)$ is differentiable at each point on the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB},$ then there exists a point $C\\in \\overset{―}{AB}$ with position vector $c$ such that\n\n$$\nf(b)-f(a)=∇f(c)·(b-a).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(b)-f(a) & =∇f(c)·(b-a) \\\\ 6-1 & =⟨{f}_{x}(c),{f}_{y}(c)⟩\\cdot (⟨2,3⟩-⟨1,2⟩) \\\\ 5 & =⟨{f}_{x}(c),{f}_{y}(c)⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1⟩ \\\\ 5 & ={f}_{x}(c)+{f}_{y}(c).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399357 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399358 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399359 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399360 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399361 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399358 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1080 #uuid "6c83438b-68cb-5418-93a9-22781afa8c79" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399357 1081 "{f}_{x}(c)+{f}_{y}(c)=4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399357 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399357 1084 #uuid "ea31dc28-2d88-5e14-a6ce-271bab6dbb95" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399358 1081 "{f}_{x}(c)+{f}_{y}(c)=5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399358 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399358 1084 #uuid "6039a47e-6f8f-5e29-ba8e-82d0b3500015" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399359 1081 "{f}_{x}(c)-{f}_{y}(c)=5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399359 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399359 1084 #uuid "81a9da62-f570-521a-b138-36cf46985648" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399360 1081 "{f}_{x}(c)-{f}_{y}(c)=4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399360 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399360 1084 #uuid "cca91f0e-0f4b-5db6-b557-f9826f488f24" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399361 1081 "{f}_{x}(c)+{f}_{y}(c)=7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399361 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399361 1084 #uuid "22f15cbc-6a53-56fd-b72f-217fe891dc5c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399362 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399363 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399362 1069 "q-98553" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399362 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399362 1071 "Let $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399362 1072 #uuid "02cd9397-a795-5b68-a5d4-f55d0d92f60a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399362 1074 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)+∇f(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)\\cdot ⟨x+1,y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)=-2.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & ={e}^{y}\\, &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{x}(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}=2, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =x{e}^{y} &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{y}(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)=-1{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =⟨2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)+∇\\,f(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩ \\\\  & =-2+⟨2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩ \\\\  & =-2+2(x+1)-2(y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2x-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399363 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399364 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399363 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399365 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399363 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399366 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399363 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399367 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399363 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399368 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399363 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399363 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399363 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399368 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399363 1080 #uuid "ecf12e78-7f08-5ce3-b44f-e89da0101f91" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399364 1081 "f(x,y)≈2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-x-y" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399364 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399364 1084 #uuid "f2803179-deb8-5b5d-8dc3-c87b7f30ccbe" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399365 1081 "f(x,y)≈2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2x+y" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399365 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399365 1084 #uuid "00a43c2f-3146-563d-a70e-8ed6a8db819c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399366 1081 "f(x,y)≈-2-x+y" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399366 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399366 1084 #uuid "06c16dd4-4550-535b-882e-e29298a652c9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399367 1081 "f(x,y)≈-2+2x-2y" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399367 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399367 1084 #uuid "1bf2d0ae-13a3-53c2-9b69-e902b7337d53" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399368 1081 "f(x,y)≈2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2x-2y" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399368 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399368 1084 #uuid "311b8139-e8df-52d9-8b84-27e1171d5a1d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399369 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399370 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399369 1069 "q-98554" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399369 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399369 1071 "Let $f(x,y,z)=xy-\\operatorname{ln}⁡z.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,1,e).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399369 1072 #uuid "f0a65ec3-c24d-50c1-a1d2-f9666a246122" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399369 1074 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,1,e)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,1,e)+∇f(1,1,e)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-1,z-e⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(1,1,e)=0.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =y\\, &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{x}(1,1,e)=1, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =x\\, &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{y}(1,1,e)=1, \\\\ {f}_{z} & =-\\frac{1}{z}\\, &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{z}(1,1,e)=-\\frac{1}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(1,1,e)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(1,1,e) & =⟨1,1,-\\frac{1}{e}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,1,e)+∇f(1,1,e)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-1,z-e⟩ \\\\  & =0+⟨1,1,-\\frac{1}{e}⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-1,z-e⟩ \\\\  & =0+1(x-1)+1(y-1)-\\frac{1}{e}(z-e) \\\\  & =-1+x+y-\\frac{z}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399370 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399371 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399370 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399372 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399370 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399373 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399370 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399374 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399370 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399375 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399370 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399370 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399370 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399371 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399370 1080 #uuid "444731d2-c3ed-5654-abe5-5731357ba09e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399371 1081 "f(x,y,z)≈-1+x+y-\\frac{z}{e}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399371 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399371 1084 #uuid "5af3dd4b-8ac7-5c57-a6e6-d30e50a37bbd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399372 1081 "f(x,y,z)≈-1-x+y-2z" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399372 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399372 1084 #uuid "be9eb651-901e-5a25-a042-03b339db014b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399373 1081 "f(x,y,z)≈1-x+y-\\frac{z}{e}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399373 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399373 1084 #uuid "75095402-2c53-53be-8b08-c572a93a18b5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399374 1081 "f(x,y,z)≈-3+x-y+\\frac{z}{e}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399374 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399374 1084 #uuid "de86e77b-b4ee-53ab-8132-4a467415d8e9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399375 1081 "f(x,y,z)≈-3+x-y-2z" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399375 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399375 1084 #uuid "f010ac91-4556-5c1a-a8d5-df7a790c142d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399377 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1069 "q-98555" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1071 "Let $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{9}{x+2y-z}.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,1,1).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1072 #uuid "ec12843c-221e-5977-accb-d9e9aa80cb79" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1074 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(2,1,1)+∇f(2,1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-1,z-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(2,1,1)=3.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =-\\frac{9}{(x+2y-z)^{2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{x}(2,1,1)=-\\frac{9}{(2+2(1)-1)^{2}}=-1, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =-\\frac{18}{(x+2y-z)^{2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{y}(2,1,1)=-\\frac{18}{(2+2(1)-1)^{2}}=-2, \\\\ {f}_{z} & =\\frac{9}{(x+2y-z)^{2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{z}(2,1,1)=\\frac{9}{(2+2(1)-1)^{2}}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(2,1,1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(2,1,1) & =⟨{f}_{x}(2,1,1),{f}_{y}(2,1,1),{f}_{z}(2,1,1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(2,1,1)+∇f(2,1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-1,z-1⟩ \\\\  & =3+⟨-1,-2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-1,z-1⟩ \\\\  & =3-1(x-2)-2(y-1)+1(z-1) \\\\  & =6-x-2y+z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399377 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399378 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399377 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399379 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399377 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399380 13194139533478 17592186045585 t